+# Aggregator Context
+
+## Role
+
+This repo exists only as a composite-build development workbench.
+
+It includes the sibling workspace repos through `includeBuild(...)` so local source changes across repos can be worked on from one Gradle entry point.
+
+## Source Of Truth
+
+- Real code lives in the sibling repos.
+- Publishing, local version movement, cleanup, and workspace refresh flows live in the root `workspace` repo.
+- This repo should stay thin: wiring, convenience tasks, and documentation only.
+
+## Expected Workflow
+
+- Use `aggregator` for cross-repo development and broad composite validation.
+- Use the actual repo directories for commits and pushes.
+- Keep this repo isolated from normal published-version orchestration.
+
+## Included Builds
+
+The composite currently expects these sibling repos:
+
+- `gradle-plugins`
+- `acme-schema-catalogue`
+- `swissknife`
+- `pillar`
+- `tools`
+- `examples`
+- `facts`
+- `modulith-example`
+- `element-service-example`
+- `lattice`
+- `quality-scorer`
